{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-49415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 5 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 & -6 \\\\  & 1 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+1}{x+3}=x+2-\\frac{5}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (x+2-\\frac{5}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+2x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "17ec6385de6f2da20b3bd5e544318d4a7480f6d4c4fa00d795c2b2a2d466a3b8"} {"question" "q-49415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}^{2}-4x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"] ["math" "2{x}^{2}-6x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+2x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+2x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x+2}{2x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+2}{2x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x+2}{2(x-\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x+2}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & 1 & 2 \\\\  & ↓ & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & 1 & \\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+2}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})} & =1+\\frac{(\\frac{7}{2})}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{7}{2(x-\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{7}{2x-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+2}{2x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1+\\frac{7}{2x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\int \\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{2x-3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x+\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{7}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "17ec6385de6f2da20b3bd5e544318d4a7480f6d4c4fa00d795c2b2a2d466a3b8"} {"question" "q-49463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{7}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C"] ["math" "x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C"] ["math" "x-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{7}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{x+1}{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x+1}{3(x+\\frac{2}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{2}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} & 1 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & 1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{2}{3})} & =1+\\frac{(\\frac{1}{3})}{(x+\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{3(x+\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{3x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int (1+\\frac{1}{3x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\int \\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[x+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "17ec6385de6f2da20b3bd5e544318d4a7480f6d4c4fa00d795c2b2a2d466a3b8"} {"question" "q-49465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{3}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C"] ["math" "x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C"] ["math" "x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-49465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-73393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x}{7x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-73393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $7$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{7x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x}{7(x+\\frac{1}{7})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\int \\frac{x}{(x+\\frac{1}{7})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{7} & 1 & 0 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & 1 & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{(x+\\frac{1}{7})} & =1+\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{7})}{(x+\\frac{1}{7})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{7(x+\\frac{1}{7})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{7x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{7x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{7x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\int \\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{7x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[x-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{7}-\\frac{1}{49}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-73393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "17ec6385de6f2da20b3bd5e544318d4a7480f6d4c4fa00d795c2b2a2d466a3b8"} {"question" "q-73393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-73393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "7x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{49}-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{7}-\\frac{1}{49}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{7}-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C"] ["math" "x-\\frac{1}{49}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-73393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x}{7}-\\frac{1}{49}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-352248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+3x+1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,\\,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-352248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $2$ |\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $3$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+3x+1}{x+2}={x}^{2}+2x-1+\\frac{3}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+3x+1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+2x-1+\\frac{3}{x+2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{1}+{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{1}-x{|}_{0}^{1}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({1}^{3}-{0}^{3})+({1}^{2}-{0}^{2})-(1-0)+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+2|) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+1-1+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{3}{2}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-352248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "17ec6385de6f2da20b3bd5e544318d4a7480f6d4c4fa00d795c2b2a2d466a3b8"} {"question" "q-352248" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-352248" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-352248" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"} {"question" "q-352248" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067994/state.json" "file_sha256" "38ba54862caadcafaed9c2cac4918808f1b2b242f515a6df68a5781c47eb38c8"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2293 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
